Z||000000||PlasticWrapd||12-05-2000||10:39 AM||||A strange thing happened the other day.  I noticed a sound like the muffler was vibrating against the "trunk" in the back when I was leaving a stop sign.  When I shifted to second, the back of the car felt like it was shaking or "waddling" back and forth.  Only does it in second gear under heavy acceleration.  Broken transmission mount?  I did a quick check on the rear tranny mount, using the lug wrench.  The mount can be move about 1/2 to 3/4" forward and backward.  Too much play?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Bob Englert||12-05-2000||05:49 PM||||That does sound like way to much play to me.  I would check ALL your mounts and the dogbone as well.  They tend to fail near the same time.<P>On most Fieros the dogbone is the first to wear out.  These are very poorly designed components IMO.  When they start getting sloppy they cause all the other mounts to work much harder.  <BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mark||12-05-2000||09:17 PM||||I agree.  Also, the front transmission mount is exposed to the heat from the cat converter.  Mine failed at about 35K miles.||||reg||1
